(a) the State-wise/UT-wise status of implementation of the National Education Policy (NEP), 2020, including progress under its key components;
(b) the State-wise/UT-wise number of schools, students and teachers covered under the NIPUN Bharat Mission, along with funds allocated, released and utilised since its launch;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of NEP, 2020 and National Initiative for Proficiency in Reading with Understanding and Numeracy (NIPUN) Bharat on foundational literacy and numeracy, learning outcomes, school attendance and dropout rates; and
(d) if so, the State-wise/UT-wise details, including key findings, performance indicators, identified gaps and corrective measures taken?

(a) the State-wise/UT-wise number of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) computerised and new multipurpose PACS established during the last three years;
(b) whether all PACS have been integrated with NABARD and Cooperative Banks through the Common ERP platform and the timeline for completion;
(c) the State-wise/UT-wise funds allocated, released and utilised under the computerisation scheme;
(d) whether Government has assessed the financial sustainability, business diversification and operational performance of PACS; and
(e) if so, the details thereof, including special assistance proposed for PACS in border and aspirational districts?

GK

(a) the details of the implementation status of the Entrepreneurship Skill Development Programme (ESDP) across the country and the outcomes achieved thereunder;
(b) details of the number of training programmes conducted and candidates trained under ESDP during the last five years, year-wise, trade-wise, State-wise and district-wise for Punjab;
(c) the details of the number of beneficiaries who have started enterprises or gained employment after completion of training under the programme, State/UT-wise, and district wise for Punjab; and
(d) the details of the funds allocated, released and utilised under ESDP during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise and district wise for Punjab?

GK

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana (PMKSY) and the PM Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) Scheme in Punjab;
(b) the project-wise details of PMKSY projects sanctioned, completed and under implementation, along with the district-wise number of beneficiaries covered under PMFME during the last three years;
(c) whether any PMKSY projects or PMFME applications are pending or delayed due to reasons attributable to the State Government if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the scheme-wise funds sanctioned, released and utilised by Punjab under both schemes, along with the corrective measures taken to ensure timely implementation?

(a) whether the Integrated Manufacturing Cluster (IMC) at Rajpura, Patiala under the Amritsar–Kolkata Industrial Corridor (AKIC) is being implemented as per the approved timeline;
(b) the present status of land acquisition, environmental clearances, trunk infrastructure works and appointment of the Programme Manager for New Cities (PMNC);
(c) whether any delay has occurred due to pending approvals or actions required from Government of Punjab; and
(d) the expected timeline for commencement of industrial allotments and the projected investment and employment generation from the project?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the progress of tourism infrastructure projects being implemented in Punjab under Swadesh Darshan 2.0, PRASHAD, the Challenge Based Destination Development (CBDD) sub-scheme and the Special Assistance to States for Capital Investment (SASCI) – Development of Iconic Tourist Centres to Global Scale Scheme;
(b) the project-wise details of proposals submitted by the State Government, indicating their present status and funds sanctioned, released and utilised;
(c) whether Government has considered developing an Integrated Sikh Heritage Circuit covering Sri Harmandir Sahib, Anandpur Sahib, Fatehgarh Sahib, Chamkaur Sahib, Khatkar Kalan and Hussainiwala; and
(d) if so, details of assistance proposed therefor?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the progress of digital connectivity initiatives in Punjab, including BharatNet and the rollout of 5G services;
(b) the district-wise details of Gram Panchayats connected in the State under BharatNet vis-à-vis the target, along with the number of 5G BTSs installed in each district;
(c) whether any implementation bottlenecks have been identified in BharatNet and whether any rural and border areas in the State still remain uncovered by broadband and mobile connectivity; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to expedite BharatNet implementation and strengthen broadband, 5G connectivity, particularly in border areas of the State?

(a) the progress made under Poshan Abhiyaan in Punjab during the last three years, including the funds sanctioned and released by Central Government;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the impact of Poshan Abhiyaan on reducing malnutrition among women and children in Punjab, and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of Working Women Hostels and One Stop Centres (Sakhi Centres) functioning in Punjab, along with Central assistance released for these facilities during the last three years; and 
(d) whether Government proposes to sanction additional Working Women Hostels and One Stop Centres in Punjab, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of households in Punjab that have benefited under the PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojana, along with the total subsidy released during the last three years;
(b) the number of biomass and compressed biogas (CBG) projects sanctioned in Punjab during the said period and the estimated quantity of paddy straw proposed to be utilised annually through these projects;
(c) whether Government proposes to provide additional incentives for expanding rooftop solar installations and promoting biomass and CBG projects, particularly to address stubble burning and enhance renewable energy generation in Punjab; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

SR

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the passenger traffic and cargo potential of Halwara (Ludhiana) airport considering Ludhiana's status as a major industrial and export hub;
(b) whether Government proposes to encourage additional airlines to commence operations from the airport and to develop dedicated air cargo facilities;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps being taken to establish Halwara airport as a major aviation hub for central Punjab?

(a) the progress made in Punjab under the Digital Agriculture Mission (DAM), including the creation of Farmer Registry, Geo-Referenced Village Maps and Crop Sown Registry;
(b) the State-wise number of Farmer IDs generated under the DAM, including Punjab, vis-à-vis the estimated number of eligible farmers in each State and Punjab's position therein;
(c) whether the comparatively low generation of Farmer IDs in Punjab has affected the integration of farmers with Central schemes and digital agricultural services; and
(d) the assistance extended to the State Government for expediting farmer registration, digital crop surveys and AI-enabled agricultural advisories?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the role of wetlands and Ramsar sites in Punjab in groundwater recharge, biodiversity conservation and climate resilience;
(b) the details of such sites notified, along with funds sanctioned and released for their conservation during the last five years;
(c) whether Government has examined the potential of wetlands in the State as natural groundwater recharge zones, particularly when groundwater extraction in the State remains above sustainable levels and many blocks continue to remain over-exploited; and
(d) whether any integrated wetland restoration and groundwater recharge programme has been proposed for Punjab in coordination with State Government?

(a) whether proposals have been received from Government of Punjab during the last five years for digitisation, preservation and AI-based archival, transcription and translation of rare Punjabi and Sikh manuscripts and for the development of museums, libraries and cultural centres in the State;
(b) the proposal-wise details thereof, indicating the funds sanctioned, released and utilised;
(c) the details of museums, libraries and cultural institutions in the State supported by the Central Government and the status of pending proposals, if any; and
(d) the steps taken to preserve endangered Punjabi manuscripts and archival materials through emerging technologies including Artificial Intelligence, digitisation and multilingual digital repositories?

(a) the details of utilisation of funds under the National AYUSH Mission (NAM) during the last five years, State-wise including Punjab;
(b) whether any AYUSH infrastructure projects sanctioned in Punjab remain incomplete and, if so, the details and reasons therefor;
(c) whether the Ministry has assessed the potential of medicinal plants cultivation in Punjab as part of crop diversification and whether Punjab has submitted any proposal under the National Medicinal Plants Board; and
(d) the details of financial and technical assistance provided or proposed to be provided by Government for strengthening AYUSH infrastructure and promoting medicinal plant cultivation in Punjab?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of water losses and irrigation inefficiencies in the State of Punjab due to ageing canal infrastructure and excessive dependence on groundwater;
(b) the details of Central assistance provided to the State under the Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana and other irrigation schemes during the last five years;
(c) whether any proposal for canal modernisation, aquifer recharge or micro-irrigation expansion from Punjab is pending with the Central Government; and
(d) steps taken by the Central Government to improve irrigation efficiency and promote sustainable water management in Punjab?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of the National Food Security Mission (NFSM), Rashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana (RKVY), Crop Diversification Programme (CDP) and National Mission on Natural Farming (NMNF) in Punjab;
(b) the district-wise area brought under maize, pulses, oilseeds and natural farming, along with the number of farmers covered under NMNF during the previous three years;
(c) whether Punjab has achieved the approved physical and financial targets under these schemes; and
(d) the scheme-wise funds released, utilised and proposals pending with the State Government?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the integration of e-Shram portal with the National Career Service (NCS) portal to enhance employment opportunities for unorganised workers;
(b) the State-wise number of workers registered on the e-Shram portal and category-wise number in Punjab, along with those linked to social security schemes;
(c) the year-wise number of jobseekers from Punjab who secured employment through the NCS Portal during the last three years and whether all employment exchanges in the State have been integrated with the NCS portal; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen convergence between e-Shram, NCS and social security schemes?

(a) whether the National Green Tribunal has recently observed that a permanent solution is required to address the pollution of Buddha Nullah in Ludhiana;
(b) the details of reports submitted by the Central Pollution Control Board and the Ministry regarding industrial discharge and compliance of Common Effluent Treatment Plants;
(c) whether the Central Government has communicated any deficiencies in implementation of the Buddha Nullah rejuvenation project to the State Government of Punjab; and
(d) the details of environmental compensation imposed on defaulting industries and the status of compliance by Government of Punjab?

(a) the number of PM SHRI Schools sanctioned and operational in Punjab;
(b) the funds sanctioned and released during the last three years;
(c) whether Government proposes to sanction additional PM SHRI Schools in Punjab; and
(d) the details thereof?

J

(a) the number of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACSs) in Punjab that have been computerised under the Central Sector Scheme, along with the funds sanctioned and released during the last three years;
(b) the number of projects sanctioned in Punjab for strengthening cooperative dairy, food processing and storage infrastructure during the said period;
(c) whether Government propose to diversify PACS into multipurpose cooperative institutions by integrating activities such as dairy, food processing, storage and other farmer-centric services, particularly in Punjab; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the quantity of Wheat and Paddy procured from Punjab during the last three years;
(b) the MSP paid to Punjab farmers during the said period;
(c) the storage capacity created in Punjab during the last three years;
(d) whether additional modern silos have been sanctioned in Punjab; and
(e) the details thereof?

(a) the details of funds sanctioned, released and utilised under the Pradhan Mantri Virasat Ka Samvardhan (PM VIKAS) Scheme in Punjab during the last three years, year-wise;
(b) the number of minority youth trained, certified and provided placement or self-employment assistance under the scheme in Punjab during the said period; and
(c) whether Government proposes to enhance the allocation under the PM VIKAS Scheme for Punjab in view of the demand for skill development and employment generation among minority communities in the State, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has prepared any roadmap for expansion of domestic and international flight operations from the newly operational Halwara (Ludhiana) airport;
(b) the details of additional domestic sectors proposed to be operationalised from Halwara airport during the next two years;
(c) whether Government has held consultations with scheduled airlines for commencing direct flights from Ludhiana to cities such as Mumbai, Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Pune and Ahmedabad; and
(d) the timeline for commencement of such services, if any?

(a) whether Government could have foreseen the damage caused by the floods in Punjab in 2025 considering the gates of Madhopur Barrage of Ranjeet Sagar Dam on River Ravi were damaged that escalated the floods;
(b) if so, the details of the steps taken in this regard;
(c) if not, the details regarding the steps taken by Government to improved prediction of such crisis in the future; and
(d) whether the Central Government has assessed the monetary damage due to Punjab floods 2025?

(a) whether Government is aware of reports highlighting disruptions in nutrition delivery and digital monitoring under Poshan Abhiyaan/Integrated Child Development Service (ICDS) in Punjab due to issues faced by Anganwadi workers and infrastructure gaps;
(b) whether concerns have been raised regarding outsourcing and quality of Take-Home Ration (THR) supply under ICDS in Punjab;
(c) details of steps taken by Government to ensure uninterrupted nutrition services, quality control of food supply, adequate digital infrastructure support to Anganwadi workers in Punjab; and
(d) whether Government proposes to undertake a third-party evaluation of ICDS/Poshan implementation in Punjab, particularly in districts with high malnutrition burden?

(a) whether it is a fact that there have been delays in infrastructure upgradation, digital facilities and teacher capacity building in PM SHRI schools identified in Punjab under the Samagra Shiksha framework;
(b) the number of PM SHRI schools approved and operationalised in Punjab vis-à-vis those where civil works, smart classrooms and skill labs have been completed;
(c) whether any gaps have been reported in utilisation of central assistance or execution capacity affecting timely implementation of PM SHRI schools in Punjab; and
(d) the corrective measures taken or proposed to ensure time-bound completion and full functionality of PM SHRI schools in Punjab?

v

(a) the number of projects sanctioned and operational under Pradhan Mantri Kisan Sampada Yojana (PMKSY) and the Pradhan Mantri Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) Scheme across the country and district wise for Punjab;
(b) total financial assistance provided under these schemes during the last three years;
(c) number of micro food processing units, Self-Help Groups (SHGs) and entrepreneurs supported under PMFME in Punjab;
(d) whether districts in Punjab have been identified under the One District One Product (ODOP) initiative and the details thereof; and
(e) steps taken by Government to strengthen food processing infrastructure and promote value addition and exports of agricultural produce from Punjab?

(a) the progress achieved under the Border Area Development Programme (BADP);
(b) the number of projects approved in border States including Punjab;
(c) the sectors covered under BADP such as roads, health, education and connectivity;
(d) whether new infrastructure projects are proposed for villages along the India-Pakistan border; and
(e) the steps taken to improve livelihood opportunities in border areas?

(a) the objectives and coverage of the Rice fortification programme under the Public Distribution System and welfare schemes;
(b) whether fortified rice containing iron, folic acid and vitamin B12 is being distributed through TPDS, ICDS and PM POSHAN schemes;
(c) the quantity of fortified rice distributed across States during the last three years;
(d) whether any quality issues have been reported regarding fortified rice supplied in Punjab; and
(e) the steps taken by Government to ensure quality standards and testing of fortified rice kernels?

v

(a) number of MSME clusters supported under schemes such as SFURTI and Cluster Development Programme, State-wise including Punjab;
(b) financial assistance provided for technology upgradation, common facility centres and marketing support to MSMEs during the last five years;
(c) whether Government has identified specific sectors such as bicycle manufacturing, auto components, textiles and sports goods for cluster development in Punjab;
(d) steps taken by Government to improve credit access to micro enterprises through schemes such as CGTMSE and Udyam registration; and
(e) whether Government proposes to integrate MSME clusters with Skill India and apprenticeship programmes to address skilled manpower shortages?

(a) whether Government is planning to formulate a central legislation or regulatory framework for regulation of fees charged by private educational institutions across the country;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the timeline for its implementation;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether it is a fact that some private schools charge readmission/annual charges from students every year in addition to tuition and other fees;
(e) if so, whether Government proposes to regulate or cap such recurring charges under any policy or regulatory mechanism; and
(f) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is considering implementation of Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) of fertilizer subsidy directly to farmers;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the proposed roadmap and timeline for rollout;
(c) the steps taken to address shortages of Di-Ammonium Phosphate (DAP) in the country; and
(d) the measures taken to correct the imbalanced NPK consumption ratio and promote balanced use of fertilizers?

(a) the number of beneficiaries trained, funds released and projects sanctioned under the PM-VIKAS (Pradhan Mantri Virasat Ka Samvardhan) scheme in the State of Punjab since inception, component-wise;
(b) whether Government has assessed the outreach of the scheme among minority artisan and traditional skill clusters in the State of Punjab, particularly in handicrafts, embroidery, leather and heritage trades; and
(c) the steps taken to enhance coverage, market linkages and livelihood outcomes for minority youth and women in the State of Punjab under PM-VIKAS?

(a) the component-wise irrigation potential created/restored, micro-irrigation area covered, watershed area developed and Central assistance released under Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana in the State of Punjab during the last five years;
(b) whether it is a fact that only about 1.52 lakh ha irrigation potential and 19, 941 ha micro irrigation has been achieved in the State so far through the scheme despite 72 per cent blocks being over-exploited; and
(c) the reasons for low PMKSY outcomes in the State compared to national achievements and the corrective roadmap for water-stressed districts of the State?

(a) the number of Mega Food Parks approved and operational in the country, specifically in Punjab;
(b) the present status of Mega Food Parks in Fazilka, Kapurthala and Ludhiana, including funds sanctioned and released;
(c) the reasons for delay in operationalisation of certain food parks in Punjab despite approvals;
(d) the employment generated and benefits accrued to farmers and MSMEs in Punjab through these parks; and
(e) whether Government proposes any special interventions to strengthen food processing infrastructure in Punjab, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the initiatives taken by Government to bolster and stimulate the growth of the startup ecosystem in Punjab;
(b) whether any measures have been implemented by Government to stimulate Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) inflows in Punjab;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) the number of startups registered, funded and operational in Punjab during the last five years, year-wise; and
(e) the steps proposed to address regional disparities, access to finance and market linkages for startups in the State?

v

(a) whether Government is aware of recent reports of violence, mob attacks and killings targeting Hindus and other religious minorities in Bangladesh, including lynching and attacks on homes, temples and businesses;
(b) the number of such incidents reported since 2024 and the specific diplomatic engagements undertaken with the Government of Bangladesh to ensure the safety and protection of minorities;
(c) whether Government has raised these concerns bilaterally or at international fora and the outcomes of such engagements; and
(d) the consular support or assistance mechanisms in place for affected Indian citizens or persons of Indian origin in Bangladesh?

(a) whether several prisoners lodged in various prisons have completed minimum prescribed sentence, including eligibility for remission and awaiting final decisions;
(b) whether it is a fact that the Sentence Review Board of Government of NCT of Delhi has, in certain cases, already recommended remission;
(c) if so, the present status of such recommendations pending with the competent authority;
(d) the number of remission cases pending with Government;
(e) details of remission given to prisoners in last five years; and
(f) whether Government proposes to issue time-bound and uniform guidelines for expeditious consideration of remission cases if so, details thereof?

(a) the total allocation and releases made to Punjab under the Agriculture Infrastructure Fund (AIF) since 2022;
(b) the number and nature of projects approved in Punjab under the scheme;
(c) whether Punjab’s requirements have been assessed in view of its major contribution to the nation's food security;
(d) the measures taken to facilitate greater access to AIF for farmer cooperatives, Farmer Producer Organisations(FPOs) and agri-entrepreneurs in Punjab; and
(e) whether any additional or special support is proposed for Punjab under the scheme?

SR

(a) whether Government is attentive towards safety concerns of Indian citizens, including workers and students, currently stranded in war-affected zones of west Asia;
(b) the estimated number of Indians affected in such conflict regions;
(c) the steps taken by Government to ensure their safety, including evacuation plans, communication support and coordination with host countries; and
(d) whether any special helpline, emergency assistance or diplomatic measures have been initiated for timely rescue and repatriation of Indian nationals from conflict zones?

bs

(a) whether the PARAKH Rashtriya Sarvekshan, 2024 indicates variations in learning outcomes across States including Punjab;
(b) the key findings relating to foundational skills and school effectiveness in Punjab;
(c) whether State-specific academic interventions are being planned based on these findings;
(d) the details of implementation of PM SHRI Schools scheme in Punjab; and
(e) the funds allocated and outcomes achieved so far under this scheme in the State?

(a) whether recent studies including NFHS-5 and ICMR-NCD reports indicate a high prevalence of hypertension, diabetes, obesity, respiratory diseases and cancer in Punjab;
(b) whether Punjab figures are above the national average for key NCD indicators;
(c) the major factors contributing to this trend;
(d) the steps taken under National Programme for Prevention and Control of Cancer, Diabetes, Cardiovascular Diseases and Stroke (NPCDCS) to strengthen screening, prevention and treatment in Punjab; and
(e) the funds allocated and utilised for Punjab during the last three years and outcomes achieved?

(a) whether Government has assessed damage to foodgrains in FCI stock, item-wise, including monetary value during the last three years;
(b) the details of foodgrain damage due to insufficient FCI godowns;
(c) steps taken to prevent such damage in future;
(d) whether there is disproportionate grain loss in Punjab due to inadequate storage infrastructure and delayed procurement operations; and
(e) wether Government proposes to strengthen cold chain and modern silos in Punjab to reduce wastage?

(a) whether AMRUT 2.0 and Swachh Survekshan 2023–24 data reflect gaps in water supply, sewerage and waste management in several urban local bodies of the State of Punjab;
(b) the status of projects approved for the State under AMRUT 2.0 and PMAY-Urban;
(c) the progress achieved so far in housing and urban services in the State;
(d) the steps taken to strengthen urban infrastructure in fast-growing towns of Punjab; and
(e) whether additional the Central support is proposed forthe State's urban transformation?

(a) whether it is a fact that there is a sustained growth in international passenger traffic from Amritsar airport, particularly to Europe, UK and Gulf sectors;
(b) details of the current cargo handling capacity and actual cargo throughput at Amritsar and Chandigarh airports;
(c) whether export potential of Punjab’s agriculture and MSME sectors has been assessed for air-cargo expansion;
(d) steps taken to strengthen cargo especially perishable handling infrastructure in Punjab;
(e) whether Government is planning to give point of call to foreign airlines under Bilateral Air Service Agreement for Chandigarh and Amritsar airport; and
(f) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is aware of the objections raised by farmer organisations and State Governments, including Punjab, regarding the proposed Seeds Bill and its implications for farmers’ traditional rights;
(b) whether the Bill proposes mandatory seed registration and greater participation of private seed companies, if so, the safeguards envisaged to prevent exploitation of farmers;
(c) whether consultations were held with Government of Punjab and farmer stakeholders prior to finalising the Bill, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to address concerns of farmers in Punjab and to ensure protection of seed sovereignty and farm livelihoods?

(a) the steps taken by Government to implement National Digital Communications Policy (NDCP) in Punjab and Gujarat;
(b) the current status of its implementation in those States, including the key targets achieved, such as broadband penetration, infrastructure development and connectivity in urban and rural areas;
(c) the funds allocated and utilized therefor and the details of future funding plans; and
(d) the initiatives taken to ensure that NDCP’s goals of providing high-speed internet, increasing broadband penetration and fostering innovation are met in those States, particularly in remote and underserved regions?

(a) whether Government is aware of multi-city higher-education study came in October, 2025 have reported 69.9 per cent students with moderate–high anxiety, 59.9 per cent depression and 70.3 per cent distress and the action plan to address such prevalence in institutions;
(b) whether it is a fact that student suicides were 7.6 per cent of total suicides (2022);
(c) if so, State-wise, details of last five years and key drivers identified;
(d) the details of year-wise funds allocated for Manodarpan initiative since its inception; and
(e) whether any impact assessment has been conducted for Manodarpan initiative and the other steps Government is planning to take for mental health of students?

(a) the details of mechanisms and frequency of drug quality testing under Central Drugs Standard Control Organization (CDSCO) random sampling processes;
(b) the details of any updates on plans to strengthen real-time tracking of drug quality issues using digital technologies;
(c) the protocols in place for ensuring quick recalls of drugs found to be substandard; and
(d) whether the Ministry is planning to bring a national standard norm for manufacturing of the medicines, so that the quality of the drugs should not vary State to State?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Ministry spent just around 4 per cent of its budget allocation of the PM Internship Scheme during April-November of Financial Year 2025-26;
(b) the details of companies enrolled in the program;
(c) the details of internship offers made to various youth since the inception of the scheme, State-wise, company-wise and year-wise;
(d) the details of internship offers accepted by youth, State-wise and company-wise; and
(e) the details of internships completed by the youth since the inception of the scheme, State-wise, company-wise and year-wise?

(a) whether Government is aware of the alarming rate of groundwater depletion in the State of Punjab;
(b) latest data on groundwater level in Punjab during the last five years, year-wise, district-wise and block-wise;
(c) whether it is a fact that Punjab Government have made multiple requests to add State of Punjab in Atal Bhujal Yojana but the State has not yet been added under the scheme and no grants received by the State under the scheme; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of youth registered and actively engaged under Mera Yuva Bharat (MY Bharat) since its launch, State-wise and district-wise for Punjab;
(b) whether any independent third-party evaluation or social audit of the scheme has been conducted;
(c) whether it is a fact that the current reporting of the scheme mainly reflects registrations rather than verified outcomes such as skills, placements or livelihoods;
(d) if so, the reasons therefor;
(e) wheather Government proposes to introduce outcome-based monitoring and publish audited impact reports; and
(f) if so, the details thereof and, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the  number of gig and platform workers registered on e-Shram portal, State-wise and district wise for the State of Punjab;
(b) whether the draft Social Security (Central) Rules, 2025, under the Code on Social Security, 2020, provides specific social security benefits for gig and platform workers and proposed timeline for their implementation;
(c) whether a dedicated Social Security Fund for such workers has been constituted and if so, its funding sources; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure mandatory onboarding of gig and platform workers by aggregator companies on e-Shram portal?

(a) whether Government is aware that despite the ongoing upgradation of Kotkapura Railway Station under the Amrit Bharat Station Scheme, Kotkapura (Faridkot) do not have the stoppage of key trains;
(b) whether the Ministry will consider approving stoppage of trains numbers 19415/19416, 19107/19108, 20497/20498 and the upcoming Firozpur–Delhi Vande Bharat at Kotkapura Junction;
(c) if so, the proposed timeline for granting these stoppages, if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether the Ministry is planning to operate new trains in Punjab; and
(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government had announced in February 2024 that a modernisation plan of ?10,000 crore for Semi Conductor Lab (SCL), Mohali was ready and proposal of the same has been sent to the cabinet;
(b) if so, the details of complete plan;
(c) whether the plan has been discussed in the cabinet;
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(e) whether there is any timeline set for the modernisation of the SCL Mohali; and
(f) if so details thereof and if not reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has conducted or plans to conduct a study on potential job losses in the country due to Artificial Intelligence (AI), especially in view of recent reports indicating significant displacement risk;
(b) if so, the details and timelines thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes measures for re-skilling and redeploying workers affected by AI;
(d) if so, the nature of such programmes; and
(e) whether Government plans to integrate AI-resilient job creation under existing employment and skilling schemes and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Ministry has selected 101 additional schools in Punjab under the PM SHRI scheme in March, 2025, in addition to the already approved 246 schools;
(b) whether approval and fund release for these 101 schools have been completed;
(c) if so, the details thereof and  if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether it is a fact that out of the 246 approved PM SHRI schools in Punjab 17 schools received zero funding in the last financial year;
(e) if so, the reasons therefor and whether they have received funding this year; and
(f) the school-wise, year-wise funding released to PM SHRI schools in  Punjab, during last five year?

(a) the total number of loans disbursed across the country under Schemes such as MUDRA, Stand-Up India, PM SVANidhi, PMEGP, CGTMSE and others during the last three years, Scheme-wise, sub-category of scheme-wise and year-wise;
(b) the number of loans disbursed in Punjab under each of these schemes during the last three years, year-wise and district-wise;
(c) whether steps have been taken to enhance awareness, accessibility and bank facilitation for entrepreneurs from Punjab, particularly women, SC/ST, minorities and rural youth; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) details of the population percentage of 6 minority communities who get benefits of various schemes of Government;
(b) whether Government is planning to introduce sub-quotas as per Supreme Court Judgement of Indra Sawhney (1992) to ensure inclusivity in scheme benefits;
(c) details of the beneficiaries of all 6 minority communities who received benefits of various schemes of Government during the last five years, year-wise, community-wise and scheme-wise;
(d) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor;
(e) whether Government is planning to exempt Minority Institutions from Property Tax; and
(f) if so, the details thereof, if not the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is providing financial assistance and technical guidance to private companies, startups and cooperatives involved in the food processing sector in Punjab through Mega Food Park, Pradhan Mantri Formalization of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) scheme or other means;
(b) if so, the district-wise and scheme-wise details of the beneficiaries and assistance provided, along with the approved list of projects and grants distributed so far;
